# globespot-layers.json

What it is: Horizon profiles of the viewpoints (plane, straight-ray globe, refracted globe)
File: src/data/dem/globespot-layers.json
SHA-256: 18646e19b7a923a6a40277026ee5cffa4c821867ef936f1c946cd094c627d3ba
Obtained: computed once by a script outside fog (research/ or scripts/).
Made by: research/lidar_horizon.py (with research/cop_dem.py and research/bev_dem.py)
From: Terrain read along each azimuth from IGN LiDAR HD (France, Licence Ouverte), Copernicus GLO-30
  (outside France) and the BEV ALS terrain model (Austria, CC BY 4.0); three curves from one reading
  of the terrain.
Licence: CC-BY-4.0 (derived from the terrain models named)
What could still be wrong: Distances along the ground come from the terrain models' coordinates: the
  radius enters there (a check, rule 10).
Used by:
- src/tabs/obs/index.js

Written by `fog build explain` from data/other.json: edit that, not this file.
